---
export const prerender = true;

import PolicyLayout from "@/components/PolicyLayout.astro";
import { appPath } from "@/lib/urls";

const accountSettings = appPath("/settings/account");

const sections = [
  { id: "operator", title: "Operator and contact" },
  { id: "accounts", title: "Accounts and sign-in" },
  { id: "projects", title: "Projects and collaboration" },
  { id: "publishing-and-git", title: "Published templates and Git" },
  { id: "assistant", title: "The AI assistant" },
  { id: "providers", title: "Storage, payments, and service records" },
  { id: "browser-storage", title: "Cookies and browser storage" },
  { id: "deletion", title: "Deletion and retention" },
  { id: "privacy-requests", title: "Privacy rights and requests" },
  { id: "policy-changes", title: "Changes to this policy" },
];
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  documentTitle="Privacy policy template | Texfolia"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="operator" aria-labelledby="operator-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="operator-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Operator and contact</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Texfolia is an online LaTeX workspace for editing documents, collaborating,
        compiling PDFs, and using a managed AI assistant.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Add the
        legal operator name, location, monitored privacy contact, and effective date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts" aria-labelledby="accounts-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="accounts-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Accounts and sign-in</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Account records include your name, email address, verification status,
        profile image when supplied, and account timestamps. Connected sign-in
        providers can supply account identifiers and authentication tokens.
        Sessions use cookies and can record your IP address, browser information,
        and an expiry time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sign-in and account-verification messages are sent by email. Cloudflare
        Turnstile checks email-code requests to help prevent abuse.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="projects-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Projects and collaboration</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Texfolia stores project names, file names, folder structure, saved text,
        uploaded files, and access permissions. Saved sources are processed to
        produce PDFs, compilation logs, and generated files. Live collaboration
        stores synchronized document state and shares presence and cursor
        information.
      </p>
      <p>
        People with project access can see its files and the names, email
        addresses, and roles shown in the collaboration panel. Personal-project
        owners manage sharing with existing accounts; organization projects use
        organization membership for access.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="publishing-and-git" aria-labelledby="publishing-and-git-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="publishing-and-git-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Published templates and Git</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Publishing a template creates a separate snapshot of saved files for
        review. Approved public templates appear in the gallery. Approved
        unlisted templates are accessible to anyone with their URL. Downloads and
        project copies are independent of the original project.
      </p>
      <p>
        Optional Git history stores repository data on Texfolia. Git commits
        record author names and email addresses. Connecting a GitHub or GitLab
        repository uses provider credentials; pushing sends committed files and
        history to that host. Unlinking discards Texfolia's repository data and
        keeps current project files. Remote copies follow the host's policies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="assistant" aria-labelledby="assistant-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="assistant-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">The AI assistant</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Using the assistant sends messages, conversation context, and project
        content read by its tools through Cloudflare AI Gateway to the selected
        model service. Tools can read and edit saved text, compile documents, and
        work with the project's Git repository. File edits are saved and shared
        with collaborators immediately.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chats are saved on the server for each user and project. Saved content
        includes messages, tool calls and results, and model reasoning when
        returned. Individual chats can be deleted from chat history. Separate
        billing records store model usage, costs, timestamps, identifiers, and
        the original payer.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Confirm
        the selected model services' retention and training practices and the
        final disclosures about AI processing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="providers" aria-labelledby="providers-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="providers-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Storage, payments, and service records</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Account and project metadata use PostgreSQL. Sources, repository
        snapshots, and generated artifacts use server storage. Cloudflare
        services provide application hosting, object storage, collaboration,
        compilation, and email delivery. Stripe processes checkout and payments;
        Texfolia stores customer and subscription identifiers and billing state.
      </p>
      <p>
        Operational logs and traces record requests, errors, compile activity,
        timing, and outcomes to help operate the service and diagnose failures.
        AI Gateway usage logs support billing reconciliation; the application
        disables Gateway request and response payload storage.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Confirm
        the production provider list, processing locations, applicable
        agreements, and disclosures about data sharing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="browser-storage" aria-labelledby="browser-storage-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="browser-storage-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p>
        Session cookies support sign-in. Your browser also stores appearance and
        editor preferences, workspace layout, and a local cache of collaborative
        text for reconnecting and offline edits. Signing out removes your
        account’s cached collaborative text and workspace layouts from the
        current browser, along with legacy recovery drafts shared across
        accounts. This includes edits that have not synchronized. The sign-out
        dialog warns before discarding these edits. Save them while connected
        before signing out. Saved documents can be downloaded again after you
        sign in. Appearance and editor preferences remain in this browser. If
        cache removal fails, Texfolia shows an error so you can retry or clear
        Texfolia's site data in your browser.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="deletion" aria-labelledby="deletion-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="deletion-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Deletion and retention</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4">
      <p>
        Deleting a project removes access and starts cleanup of saved sources,
        collaboration state, repository data, and generated artifacts. Some
        cleanup runs in background jobs and retries failures. Deleted project
        metadata and saved chat records can remain in the database. Billing
        records have a separate lifecycle and survive account or project
        deletion.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={accountSettings}>Account settings</a> includes an email-confirmed
        account deletion flow. Published templates, independent project copies,
        browser caches, and files already downloaded or pushed to a repository
        host have separate lifecycles. Removing access does not recall those
        copies.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Specify
        retention periods and deletion handling for accounts, saved chats,
        deleted metadata, logs, backups, templates, and billing records. Do not
        assume immediate erasure of every copy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy-requests" aria-labelledby="privacy-requests-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="privacy-requests-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Privacy rights and requests</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Add
        applicable privacy rights, the process for access, correction, and
        deletion requests, identity verification, and the contact responsible for
        handling requests. Confirm any statements about advertising, selling
        data, or AI training.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="policy-changes" aria-labelledby="policy-changes-heading" class="scroll-mt-8 border-t pt-8">
    <h2 id="policy-changes-heading" class="text-xl font-semibold text-balance">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 max-w-prose space-y-4 leading-7">
      <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="font-medium text-foreground">To be completed.</span> Explain
        how policy changes are dated and communicated, and add the approved
        disclosures for legal demands and business transfers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PolicyLayout>
